45585] [17592186407698 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186407698 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186407698 #edb/ref 1079 #edb/ref 17592186407693 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186407698 #edb/ref 1080 #uuid "f09bd681-f86e-50ed-9622-eb57559db7da" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186407699 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186407698 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186407699 #edb/ref 1069 "q-183340" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186407699 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186407699 #edb/ref 1071 "$\\,$ **If** $-2\\in Z,$ **then** $5$ is prime.\n\nWhich of the following statements are equivalent to the conditional statement above?\n\n- If $-2\\notin Z,$ then $5$ is not prime.\n- If $5$ is prime, then $-2\\in Z.$\n- If $5$ is not prime, then $-2\\notin Z.$" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186407699 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "23603376-708c-5de8-b4d0-019ec40ac31f" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186407699 #edb/ref 1074 "Let's recall the following facts:\n\n- The contrapositive is logically equivalent to the original statement.\n\n- The inverse and the converse are logically equivalent to each other, but not to the original statement.\n\n![](images/0d/0deb19675402bf931111bb80cb616682aac08491b5cd3e1ab5812da05b6df8a8.png)\n\nSo, we are looking for the contrapositive of the given statement.\n\n- Statement I is the inverse, not the contrapositive. $\\,\\times $\n\n- Statement II is the converse, not the contrapositive. $\\,\\times $\n\n- Statement III is the contrapositive. $\\,✓$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\"" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186407700 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186407696 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186407700 #edb/ref 1069 "q-82665" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186407700 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186407700 #edb/ref 1071 "$\\,$ **If** you are sick, **then** you are not going to school.\n\nWhich of the following statements are equivalent to the conditional statement above?\n\n- If you are not going to school, then you are sick.\n- If you are not sick, then you are going to school.\n- If you are going to school, then you are not sick." #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186407700 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "41c661ac-cdce-5cf9-814b-cfcfe49d2399" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186407700 #edb/ref 1074 "Let's recall the following facts:\n\n- The contrapositive is logically equivalent to the original statement.\n\n- The inverse and the converse are logically equivalent to each other, but not to the original statement.\n\n![](images/0d/0deb19675402bf931111bb80cb616682aac08491b5cd3e1ab5812da05b6df8a8.png)\n\nSo, we are looking for the contrapositive.\n\n- Statement I is the converse, not the contrapositive. $\\,\\times $\n\n- Statement II is the inverse, not the contrapositive. $\\,\\times $\n\n- Statement III is the contrapositive. $\\,✓$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\"" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186407701 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186407694 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186407701 #edb/ref 1069 "q-183281" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186407701 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186407701 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the inverse of the following statement: \n\n$\\,$ **If** it is not summer, **then** you don't go to the beach." #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186407701 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "a480d9fc-6f80-5af5-b6f1-0b67fa2323fc" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186407701 #edb/ref 1074 "In our conditional statement:\n\n- The antecedent is $A:$ It is not summer.\n\n- The consequent is $B:$ You don't go to the beach.\n\nThe inverse of a conditional statement $A⇒B$ is given by \n\n$$\n¬A⇒¬B.\n$$\n\nFirst, we write down the negations of $A$ and $B:$\n\n- $¬A:$ It is summer.\n\n- $¬B:$ You go to the beach.\n\nTherefore, the inverse is the following: \n\n$\\,$ If it is summer, then you go to the beach." #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186407702 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186407695 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186407702 #edb/ref 1069 "q-183274" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186407702 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186407702 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the inverse of the following statement: \n\n$\\,$ **If** $3$ divides $6,$ **then** $6$ is even." #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186407702 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "eca4be9a-a852-52a1-8e8c-2e200b9d2794" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186407702 #edb/ref 1074 "In our conditional statement:\n\n- The antecedent is $A:$ $3$ divides $6.$\n\n- The consequent is $B:$ $6$ is even.\n\nThe inverse of a conditional statement $A⇒B$ is given by \n\n$$\n¬A⇒¬B.\n$$\n\nFirst, we write down the negations of $A$ and $B:$\n\n- $¬A:$ $3$ doesn't divide $6.$\n\n- $¬B:$ $6$ is not even.\n\nTherefore, the inverse is the following: \n\n$\\,$ If $3$ doesn't divide $6,$ then $6$ is not even." #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186407703 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186407697 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186407703 #edb/ref 1069 "q-183337" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186407703 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186407703 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the contrapositive of the following statement: \n\n$\\,$ **If** ${0}⊂{1,2,3},$ **then** $4>6.$" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186407703 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "fa1fdfba-09c3-560d-b8ff-6308784b3029" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186407703 #edb/ref 1074 "In our conditional statement:\n\n- The antecedent is $A:$ ${0}⊂{1,2,3}.$\n\n- The consequent is $B:$ $4>6.$\n\nThe contrapositive of a conditional statement $A⇒B$ is given by \n\n$$\n¬B⇒¬A.\n$$\n\nFirst, we write down the negations of $A$ and $B:$\n\n- $¬A:$ ${0}⊄{1,2,3}.$\n\n- $¬B:$ $4\\le 6.$\n\nTherefore, the contrapositive is the following: \n\n$\\,$ If $4\\le 6,$ then ${0}⊄{1,2,3}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186407704 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186407705 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186407704 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "19a46d5b-7cad-5c8f-bf15-b2f08d43ce6e" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186407704 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186407700 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186407705 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186407708 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186407705 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "9864b616-65d6-5ca3-a7e3-49b7953da8ad" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186407705 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186407702 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186407706 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186407707 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186407706 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "b4ffe877-52e1-50d0-9ff6-0d5690dd67b5" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186407706 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186407703 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186407707 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "c7672cfc-51b1-5edd-a593-97ceb2928169" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186407707 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186407699 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186407708 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186407706 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186407708 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "f22856db-f661-53df-a19e-2bc1cf583961" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186407708 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186407701 #edb/ref 17592186045585]}
